WEBVTT

00:00:00.611 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:05.914
Today we start with lashes, and the first lesson is classic lashes,

00:00:05.864 --> 00:00:07.390
also called one to one:

00:00:07.645 --> 00:00:10.270
one extension on each natural lash.

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:11.550
It sounds simple.

00:00:11.895 --> 00:00:13.632
But if you want beautiful lashes,

00:00:13.582 --> 00:00:16.750
and the client's natural lashes still healthy years from now,

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:19.790
you first have to understand the natural lash itself.

00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:25.249
Natural lashes, like hair, have their own life cycle, with three phases.

00:00:25.579 --> 00:00:26.609
The growth phase:

00:00:26.878 --> 00:00:30.369
the lash gets longer, usually for about a month to six weeks.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.049
The transition phase:

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.569
the lash stops growing, and this lasts only a few weeks.

00:00:35.864 --> 00:00:38.689
Then the resting phase, which lasts several months.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.609
Finally, the lash falls out, and a new one grows in its place.

00:00:42.912 --> 00:00:44.929
The numbers vary from person to person.

00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:46.849
But what you need to remember is this:

00:00:47.191 --> 00:00:51.179
on any eyelid, at any time, there are lashes that are growing,

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:54.609
lashes that are resting, and lashes about to fall out.

00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:57.169
No two lashes are exactly alike.

00:00:57.732 --> 00:01:00.292
So losing a few lashes every day is normal.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:05.297
The extension is attached to the natural lash, so when the natural lash falls out,

00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:06.852
the extension falls with it.

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:11.972
Look closely at a shed lash, and you will see a small, pale bulb at the root.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.732
That is a natural shed:

00:01:14.071 --> 00:01:15.412
the lash had reached its time.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.172
It was not damaged by the glue.

00:01:17.426 --> 00:01:20.313
That is also why clients need to come back for refills,

00:01:20.263 --> 00:01:24.132
usually after two to three weeks, depending on how fast each person sheds.

00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:26.296
Here is something that happens a lot:

00:01:26.614 --> 00:01:30.056
new technicians attach an extension to every lash they see.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.936
Even the baby lashes, very short and very fine, just starting to grow.

00:01:35.524 --> 00:01:39.496
A baby lash is not strong enough to carry a long, thick extension.

00:01:39.921 --> 00:01:43.896
Attach one, and it is easily pulled out early, or grows in crooked.

00:01:44.163 --> 00:01:47.271
With these lashes, either leave them for the next refill,

00:01:47.221 --> 00:01:49.096
when they are longer and stronger,

00:01:49.391 --> 00:01:52.216
or choose a very short, very light extension.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:54.862
Now the golden rule of classic:

00:01:55.132 --> 00:01:59.022
one extension per natural lash, with every lash isolated.

00:01:59.763 --> 00:02:04.731
If glue sticks two natural lashes together, what people in the trade call a sticky,

00:02:04.681 --> 00:02:05.502
what happens?

00:02:05.851 --> 00:02:08.062
The two lashes grow on different schedules.

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:11.089
When one grows longer, or its time comes to shed,

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:13.502
the other holds it back and pulls it tight.

00:02:13.748 --> 00:02:16.290
The client feels something scratchy and caught,

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.782
and the lash can be pulled out before its time.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:24.062
Over time, the follicle is damaged, and the natural lashes gradually thin out.

00:02:24.728 --> 00:02:25.673
The second rule:

00:02:26.101 --> 00:02:29.273
the extension must suit the strength of the natural lash.

00:02:30.174 --> 00:02:32.473
Picture the natural lash as a small twig.

00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:36.781
Hang something too long and too heavy on it, and the twig bends,

00:02:36.731 --> 00:02:38.073
and in time it breaks.

00:02:38.496 --> 00:02:40.153
So a common guideline is:

00:02:40.356 --> 00:02:43.478
the extension is not much longer than the natural lash,

00:02:43.428 --> 00:02:45.993
and not thicker or heavier than it can carry.

00:02:46.341 --> 00:02:50.633
Fine, short natural lashes get finer, shorter extensions.

00:02:50.897 --> 00:02:51.891
As for the curl,

00:02:51.841 --> 00:02:55.905
choose it by the eye shape and the direction the natural lash grows,

00:02:55.855 --> 00:02:57.913
so the extension follows the lash,

00:02:57.972 --> 00:02:59.993
without flipping up or drooping down.

00:03:00.623 --> 00:03:01.675
The third rule:

00:03:01.826 --> 00:03:02.475
placement.

00:03:02.937 --> 00:03:06.015
The extension lies along the natural lash,

00:03:05.965 --> 00:03:09.835
with its base about 0.5 to 1 mm from the eyelid skin.

00:03:10.338 --> 00:03:11.995
It must never touch the skin.

00:03:12.347 --> 00:03:15.035
Too close, and the glue touches the eyelid:

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:19.115
the client feels scratchiness and itching, sometimes irritation.

00:03:19.464 --> 00:03:24.395
And as the lash grows, the hard bit of glue stuck to the skin pulls on the lash.

00:03:24.574 --> 00:03:29.435
Too far, and the extension is loose, sticks out, and falls off early.

00:03:30.165 --> 00:03:31.201
Now the glue.

00:03:31.595 --> 00:03:35.521
Lash glue is cyanoacrylate, from the same family as superglue.

00:03:35.779 --> 00:03:37.681
It cures with the moisture in the air.

00:03:37.948 --> 00:03:42.481
So the humidity and temperature in the room decide whether the glue cures fast or slow.

00:03:42.898 --> 00:03:46.081
Each glue maker gives a suitable humidity and temperature range:

00:03:46.348 --> 00:03:47.361
keep your room within it.

00:03:47.779 --> 00:03:52.401
In a room that is too dry, the glue cures slowly, and gives off more fumes.

00:03:52.634 --> 00:03:55.737
In a room that is too humid, it cures too fast,

00:03:55.687 --> 00:03:58.401
and the bond is brittle and holds poorly.

00:03:59.076 --> 00:04:00.897
How you take the glue matters too.

00:04:01.151 --> 00:04:03.661
Shake the bottle as the maker instructs,

00:04:03.611 --> 00:04:06.737
put one small drop on a jade stone or a glue ring,

00:04:06.926 --> 00:04:08.577
and close the bottle straight away.

00:04:08.912 --> 00:04:14.257
A drop left out too long thickens and bonds poorly, so change to a fresh drop often.

00:04:14.814 --> 00:04:19.364
When you dip, dip only the base of the extension, with just enough glue,

00:04:19.314 --> 00:04:20.177
never a blob.

00:04:20.494 --> 00:04:25.115
The fumes sting the eyes, so the client's eyes must stay fully closed throughout,

00:04:25.065 --> 00:04:27.937
and never keep the glue drop right under her nose.

00:04:28.435 --> 00:04:32.437
The fumes can also cause allergies, for both the client and the technician,

00:04:32.387 --> 00:04:36.337
and you will find this in detail in the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:04:36.873 --> 00:04:39.394
Before you start, always look and ask.

00:04:39.650 --> 00:04:44.774
Red, itchy or watery eyes, a stye, a swollen or crusty lash line,

00:04:44.724 --> 00:04:48.834
recent eye surgery, or a past reaction to lash glue:

00:04:48.944 --> 00:04:50.034
then not today.

00:04:50.461 --> 00:04:53.183
For the full list, and how to say no kindly,

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:55.794
see the lesson on when not to do a service.

00:04:56.331 --> 00:04:58.835
Never treat the consultation as a formality.

00:04:59.088 --> 00:05:00.915
Ask what look the client wants:

00:05:01.014 --> 00:05:03.235
very natural, or a little fuller.

00:05:03.663 --> 00:05:09.230
Ask whether she wears contact lenses, whether she often swims or uses the sauna,

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:10.195
rubs her eyes,

00:05:10.386 --> 00:05:12.195
or sleeps face down on the pillow.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:15.315
These habits decide how long the lashes last.

00:05:15.664 --> 00:05:17.395
Then explain aftercare up front:

00:05:17.698 --> 00:05:21.316
keep the lashes dry for as long as the glue maker advises,

00:05:21.266 --> 00:05:23.715
no oil based products at the lash base,

00:05:23.909 --> 00:05:27.103
brush them every day, no rubbing, no pulling them out,

00:05:27.053 --> 00:05:29.315
and a refill after two to three weeks.

00:05:29.983 --> 00:05:32.914
And finally, be honest with the client about classic.

00:05:33.177 --> 00:05:37.234
Classic gives a natural look, like a very well applied coat of mascara.

00:05:37.738 --> 00:05:40.114
Thick natural lashes give a thick result.

00:05:40.462 --> 00:05:44.754
Sparse natural lashes stay sparse with classic, just longer and darker.

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:50.116
If the client wants really full, dramatic lashes, that is a different technique,

00:05:50.066 --> 00:05:51.154
volume or hybrid,

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:52.994
which we will learn in later lessons.

00:05:53.329 --> 00:05:57.874
Never attach very thick, very long extensions just to please the client.

00:05:58.242 --> 00:06:00.914
Because it is her natural lashes that pay the price.

00:06:01.587 --> 00:06:02.288
So you see.

00:06:02.717 --> 00:06:05.088
Classic lashes are not hard on the hands.

00:06:05.275 --> 00:06:06.768
They are hard on your patience:

00:06:07.114 --> 00:06:10.733
isolate exactly one lash, choose an extension it can carry,

00:06:10.683 --> 00:06:12.608
place it a little off the skin,

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:15.008
and never let two lashes stick together.

00:06:15.347 --> 00:06:17.728
Once you understand, your hands will follow.

00:06:18.147 --> 00:06:21.328
In the practice lesson, we'll go through it step by step together.

00:06:21.592 --> 00:06:24.048
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:25.088
See you next time.
